  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Physical Properties
    
    A fire-core tome bound in volcanic glass and ancestor bone, owned by the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, a shadow parliament of fire-keepers and guild-masters rooted in Nightfall Shelf's volcanic depths. The binding is shadow-steel reinforced with femur-carved clasps. The pages — compressed volcanic ash and bioluminescent fungal pulp — are warm to the touch, a heat that persists beyond the exhaustion cycle of any fire-core crystal ever mined. The text glows faintly in absolute darkness but burns away under aurora-light, a property the Nightshelf considers a feature. A permanent frost-crack runs through the back cover where someone attempted to burn the tome during the Clever Ice Age; the Covens' Order will not identify who. The spine bears three deliberate notches, one for each reader who did not return.
    
    ## Discovery and Naming
    
    The tome was recovered from an unmapped tunnel below the mid-galleries during the Faction Wars by Augur ☽'Silvsiaelrous~ the Resolute, a Nightshelf scholar and deep-reader, and a tunnel-runner named ☽'profundius. It rested on a shelf of natural basalt in a pocket chamber of layered volcanic glass — deliberately placed, by all appearances, before the deep froze shut. Silvsiaelrous spent what the chronicle *Three Days* records as three hours in total darkness reading bioluminescent script that described everything beneath the ice predating penguin civilization, including fire-knowledge and forge-patterns later connected to forbidden deep-pressure workings. She carried the tome to Nightfall Shelf, where the Order's archivists assigned it the designation ☽'somunis' Mist~Record.
    
    The first notch in the spine is hers.
    
    ## The Three Readers
    
    Every complete reader of the Mist~Record has either vanished into the tunnels or refused to speak again. Under Mandatum∴ccord — the Nightshelf's binding law of witnessed testimony — each reader's fate is documented in a separate ledger that has grown thicker than the tome itself.
    
    The second notch was carved for a reader whose name the records preserve but no one repeats. The third belongs to an unnamed reader who entered the vault during a Long Dark and did not emerge. The bioluminescent cloth wrapping the tome was found refolded in their absence.
    
    ## Custody
    
    The tome is stored in a shadow-forge vault beneath ☽'shadow Samsiavae~, a deep-tunnel fire-mine below Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius, wrapped in bioluminescent cloth that has never been changed. The last penguin to request a reading was a scholar named Tuk'krek. Tuk'krek's daughter guarded the vault for eleven seasons without opening the cloth. Custody then passed to her granddaughter ☽'laestiala, keeper by default, who reported to the shadow-parliament that the artifact was intact without ever unwrapping it. The cloth remains folded exactly as Tuk'krek left it.
    
    The Midnight Claws — a faction that once controlled the tunnels surrounding the sanctuary — served as earlier custodians before their dissolution. The ☽'ofund' Guild Registry archives cross-reference the tome for relic designations connected to the Vum∴tenebra, the conflagration at Terrace Momiou during the Flipper Accord's collapse, though the relevant entry is sealed.
    
    ## The Scar-Mouth Song
    
    Fire-tenders on deep shifts below Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius sing fragments of a tunnel-song called 'The Scar-Mouth Song,' which encodes warnings about the tome in work-chant melody. No complete version survives. Parts of the refrain are attributed to a courier named ☽'voidae, who disappeared during the Flipper Accord's seventh renegotiation. The refrain is considered unlucky to sing above mid-depth. The surviving verses half-mourn the Midnight Claws' absence without admitting it.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
