  annotation "note_1771576309811_2", anchor: "reported to the shadow-parliament that the artifact was intact without ever unwrapping it", text: "Three generations. Tuk'krek read. His daughter guarded eleven seasons without opening. Her daughter reported it intact without unwrapping. Each generation moved further from the act that defined the first. This is how knowledge dies on the Berg — not destroyed but swaddled, passed flipper to flipper by keepers increasingly certain that safety means distance. The cloth remains folded. The cloth will always remain folded. And the three notches in the spine will stay at three, which is the kindest thing anyone has done for this tome or for anyone else.", type: :commentary, display: :full
